<GuideLayout 
  title="Hybrid Sourcing: Balancing Ready-to-Ship with Custom OEM Designs"
  type="STRATEGY"
  date="June 29, 2026"
  readTime="15 min read"
>
  <p>The most successful activewear brands in the current market don't choose between "Ready-to-Ship" and "Custom OEM"—they utilize both. This hybrid sourcing strategy allows for speed-to-market while maintaining brand exclusivity.</p>
  
  <h2>Why Ready-to-Ship for Private Label?</h2>
  <p>For seasonal trends or quick inventory refreshes, our <strong>Ready-to-Ship (RTS)</strong> program with custom branding is the gold standard. It allows you to add your logo to proven silhouettes with an MOQ as low as 50 pieces, significantly reducing your inventory risk.</p>
  
  <h2>When to Pivot to Custom OEM</h2>
  <p>As your brand matures, unique tech packs and custom colors become your competitive edge. Our <strong>OEM Manufacturing</strong> services allow for total control over fabric development, custom hardware, and specialized patterns with an MOQ of 150-200 pieces.</p>
  
  <h2>The FITCLO Roadmap</h2>
  <p>We recommend our clients start with a 70/30 split: 70% proven RTS styles to ensure cash flow, and 30% exclusive OEM designs to build brand identity. This balanced approach ensures you are never out of stock on essentials while always offering something new and unique to your loyal customers.</p>
</GuideLayout>
